      "id": "luowulc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Need for Classification of Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Dobereiner grouped elements into Triads where the central element's atomic mass was approximately the average of the other two.",
        "Newlands proposed the Law of Octaves, observing that every eighth element possessed similar physical and chemical properties up to calcium.",
        "Mendeleev arranged elements in order of increasing atomic mass and predicted the properties of undiscovered elements like Eka-aluminium and Eka-silicon.",
        "Henry Moseley established that atomic number, rather than atomic mass, is the fundamental property governing periodic trends.",
        "Atomic radius decreases across a period from left to right due to increased nuclear charge and increases down a group."
      ],
      "id": "2wfcuqf"
    },
